  "worked_solution": "The object is decelerating when its acceleration is negative. In a speed-time graph, the acceleration is given by the slope of the line.\n\nThe line passes through the points $(30,10)$ and $(50,5),$ so its slope is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{5\\text{\u00a0m/s}-10\\text{\u00a0m/s}}{50\\text{\u00a0s}-30\\text{\u00a0s}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5\\text{\u00a0m/s}}{20\\text{\u00a0s}} \\\\  & =-0.25\\,\\frac{\\text{m}}{{\\text{s}}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the acceleration of the object is $-0.25\\,\\text{m}/{\\text{s}}^{2},$ which means that the deceleration of the object is $0.25\\,\\text{m}/{\\text{s}}^{2}.$",
